---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How WizardLoop handles feedback, local preferences, optional Telegram embeds and information processed by hosting and security providers."
>
  <section class="wrap prose-page">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE SMALL PRINT</p>
      <h1>
        Your privacy,
        <br />
        in plain language.
      </h1>
      <p>
        WizardLoop is my personal creative website. This notice explains what
        happens when you visit, load optional content or get in touch.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reviewed <time datetime="2026-10-27">27 October 2026</time>.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Visiting the website</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. I do not run advertising, visitor
        analytics or a marketing mailing list here. Hosting providers still
        process connection information, such as an IP address and browser
        details, to deliver and protect the website. GitHub describes its
        processing in the{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
          GitHub Privacy Statement
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <p>
        Your browser can remember your theme, motion and optional
        Telegram-content preferences in local storage. These preferences are not
        sent to a visitor analytics service. See the{' '}
        <a href="/cookies/">Cookie &amp; Storage Policy</a> for controls.
      </p>

      <h2>Feedback and direct contact</h2>
      <p>
        When the feedback service is enabled, the form asks for your name and
        message. Your email is optional. I use those details to read your
        feedback and, when possible, respond to your request. You do not need to
        submit feedback to browse this website.
      </p>
      <p>
        The form sends your information through a separate Cloudflare service to
        a private Telegram conversation with me. The delivered message includes
        your submitted details, the source page and a receipt time. It does not
        include your IP address. The service does not maintain a separate
        database of feedback messages or log their contents.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cloudflare Turnstile and rate limiting help prevent automated abuse.
        Cloudflare processes technical connection information for those checks.
        The rate limiter uses a daily-changing, secret-derived identifier based
        on the connection IP; this identifier is not sent to Telegram. Turnstile
        is used only for feedback when configured, with an explanation before it
        loads. Read{' '}
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">
          Cloudflare's Privacy Policy
        </a>{' '}
        for its provider-level processing.
      </p>
      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          Availability is shown on the feedback page. An unconfigured form does
          not send messages. A local mock explicitly states that nothing was
          sent to Telegram. A live delivery is only reported as successful after
          the service receives a success response.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        If you choose email or Telegram instead, the provider you use also
        processes that conversation. Avoid sending information that is
        unnecessary for your request.
      </p>

      <h2>Optional Telegram content</h2>
      <p>
        Telegram post embeds are not loaded until you choose to enable them.
        Loading an embed connects your browser to Telegram, which can receive
        connection information and use its own storage or cookies. Opening a
        Telegram link also takes you to its service. See the{' '}
        <a href="https://telegram.org/privacy">Telegram Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can decline embeds and use the original post links. You can also
        withdraw the website's stored Telegram preference from the{' '}
        <a href="/posts/">Posts page</a>. This stops further embedding here; it
        cannot undo data already received by Telegram or clear cookies owned by
        Telegram.
      </p>
      <p>
        <button class="button" type="button" data-privacy-open>
          Manage external content
        </button>
      </p>

      <h2>Keeping and deleting information</h2>
      <p>
        Your browser preferences remain until you change or clear them. Feedback
        sent to me remains in the private Telegram conversation until I delete
        it. There is currently no automatic deletion schedule. I review requests
        for deletion and keep information only where it remains necessary to
        handle the conversation or an applicable legal obligation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Provider security records, backups and service retention are governed by
        the providers' own policies. Information may be processed in countries
        other than your own. I cannot promise immediate removal from a
        provider's independent records or backups.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can browse without submitting feedback, decline external embeds,
        remove browser preferences and contact me about information you have
        provided. Where applicable data-protection law grants rights of access,
        correction, deletion, restriction, objection or portability, you can
        make a request using the contact details below. I may need limited
        information to identify the relevant message and confirm that the
        request is yours.
      </p>
      <p>
        The purpose of feedback processing is to handle your requested
        communication; security processing protects the service from abuse.
        Optional embeds load based on your choice. Any legal basis and
        obligations depend on the applicable circumstances. This notice does not
        claim an exemption from Israeli or European privacy law or certify legal
        compliance. For general information, the European Commission explains{' '}
        <a href="https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-topic/data-protection/information-business-and-organisations/dealing-requests-individuals_en">
          requests to exercise data-protection rights
        </a>
        . You may also contact the competent data-protection authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact WizardLoop</h2>
      <p>
        For a privacy question or deletion request, email{' '}
        <a href="mailto:wizard@wizardloop.com">wizard@wizardloop.com</a> or{' '}
        <a href="https://t.me/wizardloop">contact me on Telegram</a>. Include
        enough context to locate your message, without sending unrelated
        personal information.
      </p>
      <p>
        This notice will be updated if the website's services or data practices
        change.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
